The tourist is one of the more difficult classes to play. Perhaps you
should try a valkyrie first, or some other easy class.

> I've played tourists before with similiar life expectencies.  I'm
> thinking about putting on the first bits of armour I can.  It seems
> that cursed -2 chainmail is better than nothing.

It isn't. Once you find better armour, you can't take it off. Perhaps what
you're doing works for other armour than body armour, though. If you're
stuck with a hard had, tough luck, but it doesn't weigh that much. Body
armour easily encumbres a tourist, so you can hardly carry anything useful
or become encumbered.

> The same with
> weapons.  I've reached the point where I could enhance unarmed combat
> before finding any kind or sword and an altar to check for cursedness.

You don't need an altar for that. Keep your pet alive and see if it will
step on your weapon. If it won't, it's cursed. If your pet *does* step on
an item, without you getting the message that it does so "reluctantly",
it's not cursed.

Keeping your pet alive has the added benefit that it can fight in your
place. Your pet is a lot stronger than you are, at least in the beginning.

